Add an `inhibit-idle` window rule (upstream PR YaLTeR/niri#2373).

Lets a window keep the idle notifier from firing, either unconditionally
(`inhibit-idle "always"`) or only while it is fullscreen
(`inhibit-idle "fullscreen"`). `inhibit-idle null` explicitly clears the rule
again for a later, more specific match.

Source: https://github.com/ppenguin/niri/tree/inhibit_idle
Regenerated against the niri-unstable rev pinned in this flake's lock so it
applies without fuzz; refresh it from that branch when it stops applying.
